记录在案 On the Record — Tech Launch (科技发布), a NEO-Cine library demo

PRODUCT AND INTERFACE: 建造观察局 (BITBUILD), https://news.bitbuild.cc, the library author's own website.
  Every interface in the film is a page of the site frozen on 2026-11-14 with ../kit/tools/freeze.mjs: its DOM, CSS, images
  (company and article covers) and fonts, unchanged; the film only enlarges, clones and moves them. Nothing is redrawn.
  Facts on screen: FACTS.md. The frozen pages (site/) are made by the build and not kept in git.
  The site's own fonts, served by the site and used as they are inside the interface: Archivo and IBM Plex Mono (both SIL OFL 1.1)
  and the site's own serif (a subset made for the site); Chinese body text in the site's system font stack (PingFang SC on macOS,
  Microsoft YaHei on Windows).

FILM'S OWN FONTS (SIL Open Font License 1.1; fetched by ../kit/tools/fonts.py from github.com/google/fonts at commit 86aced91 into
  out/fonts-src/, subset to the characters the film prints into fonts/*.ttf; none kept in git; licence texts in fonts/):
- Instrument Serif, (c) 2022 The Instrument Serif Project Authors: English titles and figures (fonts/IS.ttf).
- Noto Sans SC, (c) 2014-2021 Adobe (http://www.adobe.com/), with Reserved Font Name 'Source': Chinese titles, notes, cards
  (fonts/NSC-500.ttf, fonts/NSC-700.ttf, instances of the variable font).
- JetBrains Mono, (c) 2020 The JetBrains Mono Project Authors: frame type, eyebrows, kickers, the address (fonts/JBM.ttf).

SOUND: synthesized in code, no recordings or samples. Score: ../kit/tools/score.mjs (D major, 100 BPM, from the page's events);
  effects: ../kit/tools/sfx_synth.mjs (eight sounds); mix: ../kit/tools/mix.py. No narration.

STYLE AND CODE: adapted from the Tech Company theme (主题-科技公司式) of the NEO Product Promo skill (neo-product-promo,
  MIT, (c) 2026 NEO造物集 (neohoy), the library author): the page logic (window, frozen pages, floating components, Canvas marks),
  the time plan, the score and the effects, and the freeze, explore, login and screenshot tools. What changed for the library is
  listed at the top of each file in ../kit/. GSAP and HyperFrames, which the skill used, are not used or shipped: text entrances
  are evaluated by ../kit/page/tween.js, adapted from Scrapbook Song's gsap-lite.js.

TOOLS: the NEO-Cine library's core/ tools, which are Lemo-Opuscar's (MIT, (c) 2026 LemoLab): headless Chrome frame capture,
  events export, reading-time check, ffmpeg encode and loudness master; neo/audio/cues.py, neo/audio/master.py,
  neo/render/remote.sh.

ON SCREEN: the brand's own end card (the blue square, 建造观察局, the address) is part of the film's content; the last card signs
  off with NEO-Cine and the style's name only.
